# Local settings for `pnpm dev`. Copy to .env (git-ignored). Every variable
# is validated in src/env.ts.
PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=info
# All state: site.db and the published site (public/). Back up through the CLI.
DATA_DIR=./data
# Where backup archives go: a separate disk, copied off the machine (restic).
# Defaults to DATA_DIR/backups, on the site's own disk.
# BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/ftds-site-builder
# The daily backup's Malaysian time, HH:MM, or off.
# BACKUP_SCHEDULE=02:00
# Archives kept: the newest of each of this many days, and of this many weeks.
# BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY=7
# BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY=4
# The built admin app, served at /admin. In development Rsbuild serves it on :3001.
# ADMIN_DIST=../admin/dist
# The builder's own public address, which agents connecting over MCP sign in
# against (docs/mcp.md). Without it, each request's address is used: behind a
# proxy that needs TRUST_PROXY, or agents are sent to http:// addresses.
# BUILDER_URL=https://builder.agensi.gov.my
# Public address of the published site; enables sitemap.xml.
# SITE_URL=https://www.agensi.gov.my
# Largest upload the media library accepts, in MB.
# MEDIA_MAX_MB=10
# Behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy), its address, so the server believes
# what it says: that the request came over HTTPS (the sign-in cookie is only
# marked Secure then) and the visitor's address (the audit log, the sign-in
# limits, analytics). A hop count or addresses and CIDRs (10.0.0.0/8,127.0.0.1).
# Avoid true, which believes any client's X-Forwarded-For.
# TRUST_PROXY=127.0.0.1
# A MaxMind-format country database, so analytics can list countries.
# GEOIP_DB=./data/dbip-country-lite.mmdb
# The first account: on a boot where there's no super admin yet, these make
# one, which must change its password at first sign-in. After that they're
# ignored and can be removed. Required for a new install.
# SUPER_ADMIN_USERNAME=pentadbir
# SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=at-least-12-characters
